"Slow" is the very essence of your problem; with a wizard, you need to
press on.  Nothing kills wizards anything like as surely as gaining too
many levels too shallow in the dungeon does.  Wizards need gold (for
divine protection) and organic armour and magic items, especially magic
items that incapacitate or otherwise distract the enemy rather than
killing them (potions of paralysis or blindness or confusion, wands of
sleep, wands of teleportation).  You don't find these things by
progressing slowly, since low-level monsters very rarely have treasure;
you find them by exploring a level and moving on.  And my wizards don't
rely on their pets for identification anything like as much as they rely
on their pets to *kill things*!  And your pet gets better at killing
things the more things it kills.

I repeat: a cat or dog that's gained some experience is immensely
valuable to *anyone* in the early game, and a major part of the key to
success with weak characters like wizards and healers.

